  "operations": {
    "group_allowed_paths_by_repo": "git_snapshot.group_allowed_paths_by_repo(workspace, allowed_paths, external_roots): maps each allowed path to its canonical containing repository root at path-resolution level only. Relative entries map to the main workspace; absolute entries map to their Git repository. Trusted roots are not consulted. An absolute entry outside any Git repository raises ValueError.",
    "scope_match": "git_snapshot.is_allowed/scope_violations on one already-normalized scope and one candidate path: file entries match exactly, directory entries (trailing slash) match strict descendants only. This corpus exercises only the pure path predicate, not change detection.",
    "symlink_identity": "A single symlink is captured with git_snapshot.take_snapshot and then compared after retargeting with git_snapshot.changed_paths. It isolates the symlink target identity (lstat/readlink digest) and the resulting scope verdict; it is not the general changed/status/index/HEAD comparison corpus.",
    "validate_allowed_paths": "git_snapshot.validate_allowed_paths(workspace, allowed_paths, external_roots): returns normalized scope paths or raises ValueError. Relative entries stay workspace-relative and may not escape lexically or through a symlink; absolute entries must resolve inside a trusted root and belong to a Git repository whose root is also inside a trusted root."
  },
